WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.753 --> 00:00:18.439
The sun had set, and tiny bugs darted around the back-porch light.

2
00:00:19.699 --> 00:00:24.841
Mom put a baseball cap on Katie's head and said, "The air is getting cool."

3
00:00:26.002 --> 00:00:28.883
Luke tied a big rag onto Katie's belt loop.

4
00:00:30.384 --> 00:00:31.244
"What's that for?"

5
00:00:31.712 --> 00:00:32.412
Katie asked.

6
00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:35.474
"You'll see," said Luke.

7
00:00:35.494 --> 00:00:37.155
"Do you have your bucket?"

8
00:00:37.175 --> 00:00:39.576
"Yep," said Katie.

9
00:00:39.596 --> 00:00:44.419
"Flashlight?" "Yep," replied Katie.

10
00:00:44.439 --> 00:00:46.580
"I'm ready to hunt worms."

11
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:51.022
"Don't go too far from the house," said Mom.

12
00:00:51.042 --> 00:00:53.063
"And don't be gone long!"

13
00:00:54.184 --> 00:00:57.666
Katie and Luke stepped off the porch and headed into the darkness.

14
00:00:57.686 --> 00:01:01.288
"The grass is all wet," said Katie.

15
00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.561
"That's good," explained Luke.

16
00:01:04.581 --> 00:01:07.862
"Earthworms like it cool and wet."

17
00:01:07.882 --> 00:01:12.264
"My toes don't," replied Katie.

18
00:01:12.804 --> 00:01:14.325
Her sneakers felt soggy.

19
00:01:14.345 --> 00:01:17.727
"Walk softly," warned Luke.

20
00:01:17.747 --> 00:01:22.629
"If they feel our footsteps, they will slip right back into the ground."

21
00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:26.770
"I thought we had to dig for worms," said Katie.

22
00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:30.332
"That's the hard way," replied Luke.

23
00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:32.369
"This is the easy way."

24
00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:35.951
They stepped carefully through the grass.

25
00:01:37.092 --> 00:01:41.614
There was no sound except the croaking of the toads down by the creek.

26
00:01:42.675 --> 00:01:45.496
"Okay, stop here," instructed Luke.

27
00:01:45.516 --> 00:01:47.477
"Turn on your flashlight."

28
00:01:48.598 --> 00:01:51.760
Katie flashed the red beam back and forth over the grass.

29
00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:54.601
"See," he whispered.

30
00:01:54.621 --> 00:01:56.522
"The worms are out!"

31
00:01:58.043 --> 00:01:58.884
Luke was right!

32
00:02:00.184 --> 00:02:04.528
Everywhere the light shone, Katie could see worms gleaming in the grass.

33
00:02:04.548 --> 00:02:08.812
"Ooh, creepy," she whispered.

34
00:02:09.973 --> 00:02:11.074
Luke gave her a look.

35
00:02:11.094 --> 00:02:13.916
"Sorry," said Katie.

36
00:02:13.936 --> 00:02:17.059
"I mean, ooh, cool!"

37
00:02:17.079 --> 00:02:21.023
"Now watch me," ordered Luke.

38
00:02:22.224 --> 00:02:25.347
He bent over one of the shining worms and grabbed it.

39
00:02:27.104 --> 00:02:30.266
Then he slowly pulled the worm out of its hole.

40
00:02:30.286 --> 00:02:32.927
"Got it," said Luke.

41
00:02:32.947 --> 00:02:34.628
"It's a big one."

42
00:02:35.168 --> 00:02:36.689
He plopped it into his bucket.

43
00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:38.410
"Now you try."

44
00:02:39.911 --> 00:02:43.853
Katie stooped down beside Luke and quickly spotted an earthworm.

45
00:02:44.974 --> 00:02:46.694
She reached out and grabbed.

46
00:02:46.714 --> 00:02:48.175
"Got it!"

47
00:02:48.656 --> 00:02:49.136
she said.

48
00:02:49.716 --> 00:02:51.597
She held her hand up to show Luke.

49
00:02:52.618 --> 00:02:54.058
But her hand was empty.

50
00:02:54.078 --> 00:02:55.679
"It got away!"

51
00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:56.800
she cried.

52
00:02:57.404 --> 00:02:59.205
"And my hand is all slimy!"

53
00:02:59.225 --> 00:03:03.347
"That's what your rag is for," explained Luke.

54
00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:06.408
"Dry your hand and try again.

55
00:03:06.988 --> 00:03:09.669
This time, grab it closer to the middle."

56
00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:14.611
As Katie wiped her hand on her rag, she spotted another worm.

57
00:03:15.832 --> 00:03:20.033
She slowly stretched out her hand and grabbed it around its middle.

58
00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:21.174
She pulled.

59
00:03:21.194 --> 00:03:23.575
"It won't come out.

60
00:03:23.935 --> 00:03:26.056
It's holding on," she said.

61
00:03:27.168 --> 00:03:29.309
"Keep pulling," instructed Luke.

62
00:03:29.329 --> 00:03:31.790
"The worm will get tired and let go."

63
00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.711
Katie pulled some more until the earthworm came sliding out.

64
00:03:36.731 --> 00:03:40.092
"Hooray!" she exclaimed.

65
00:03:40.112 --> 00:03:41.793
"I got one!"

66
00:03:41.813 --> 00:03:44.694
"Okay," said Luke.

67
00:03:44.714 --> 00:03:46.454
"Toss it in the bucket."

68
00:03:47.895 --> 00:03:52.016
A little later, Katie and Luke ran through the back door, into the kitchen.

69
00:03:53.324 --> 00:03:58.148
Everyone was sitting around the table, and Grandpa was serving slices of apple pie.

70
00:03:58.168 --> 00:04:00.349
"I've got worms!"

71
00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:01.770
shouted Katie.

72
00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:04.992
"Not in the house," said Mom.

73
00:04:05.012 --> 00:04:08.094
"Oh, right," said Katie.

74
00:04:08.675 --> 00:04:11.697
She opened the back door and set her bucket on the porch.

75
00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:18.181
"Now, before you have your pie," said Mom, "why don't you show Luke our new chicks?"

76
00:04:19.342 --> 00:04:20.263
Katie sighed.

77
00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.301
She wanted to talk about her worms.

78
00:04:24.321 --> 00:04:28.343
"Come on, Luke," she said softly.

79
00:04:28.883 --> 00:04:32.064
Katie led her cousin out of the kitchen and up the stairs.

80
00:04:33.285 --> 00:04:37.586
She opened the door to the spare room and pulled him over to the chick box.

81
00:04:37.606 --> 00:04:40.587
"There they are," she said.

82
00:04:40.608 --> 00:04:43.829
"They're cute, but a lot of trouble.

83
00:04:44.329 --> 00:04:47.450
You have to feed them and clean up their stinky poop."

84
00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:51.432
"Worms are more fun," stated Luke.

85
00:04:52.524 --> 00:04:54.986
"That's for sure," agreed Katie.

86
00:04:55.006 --> 00:04:57.248
"Now, let's go eat some pie."

87
00:04:58.489 --> 00:05:01.972
The two worm hunters didn't notice another hunter in the hallway.

88
00:05:03.153 --> 00:05:05.995
Jellybean had been waiting silently in the dark.

89
00:05:07.496 --> 00:05:09.498
She crept toward the spare room.

90
00:05:10.619 --> 00:05:13.301
The door had been left open just a crack.

91
00:05:13.902 --> 00:05:17.184
Jellybean put one paw on the door and pushed.

92
00:05:19.246 --> 00:05:23.331
The chicks chirped inside their box as the door swung open.
